 "details": {
  "title": "It Was Almost Like a Song",
  "lead": "It Was Almost Like a Song in B, the way Johnny Hartman sings it on his 1980 record, for trumpet an octave above his voice: concert E3 to C♯5 (F♯ to D♯ for the trumpet). The bars are the Fret Finder page’s, which follow his record, so the line goes with the guitar track there. He sings out of time and the bars stretch with him; the lights follow his timing. His turns, scoops and quick notes on the way down sit in small boxes over the note they belong to, to play or leave out.",
  "facts": [
